infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Materialize the array vs pull through generators
  desc Peak memory transforming 10M rows averaging ~150 bytes
  compares
    - label Eager array
      children
        - label Peak memory ~1.5 GB
          desc 10M rows x ~150 bytes buffered as one live array
        - label Every stage reallocates
          desc Each .map/.filter materializes another full array
        - label O(N) in row count
          desc Memory scales with the export, not the batch
        - label Full cost paid up front
          desc No backpressure; the pod OOMs before the first write
    - label Lazy generator pipeline
      children
        - label Peak memory ~4 objects
          desc One item live per stage, not ten million
        - label source -> filter -> map -> sink
          desc One row flows through; nothing buffers between stages
        - label O(1) in row count
          desc Stream a result set larger than RAM
        - label Backpressure for free
          desc A slow sink.write throttles the DB cursor end to end
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
